IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpc-types`

-- Criminal Procedure Code 2010, Second Schedule "Laws to which criminal case disclosure procedures apply" (sections 159(1), 211A(1)
-- and 427(1)), with sections 159 and 211A that read it.
-- Source: source/CPC2010.txt lines 21838 to 21919 (the Schedule), 7307 to 7321 (s 159), 7885 to 7905 (s 211A).
--
-- The question this module answers: DO THE CRIMINAL CASE DISCLOSURE PROCEDURES APPLY TO THIS OFFENCE?  The procedures are the
-- Case for the Prosecution and Case for the Defence exchange of Part 9 Division 2 (State Courts) and Part 10 Division 5 (the General
-- Division of the High Court).  The Schedule lists WRITTEN LAWS, not offences: an offence is within it when it is created by one of the
-- listed Acts (the whole Act, unless the item says otherwise).  Section 159 then asks where the offence is to be tried; section 211A asks
-- whether it must be, or the Public Prosecutor has designated that it be, tried in the High Court.  The Schedule is NOT the First Schedule
-- (the Penal Code's procedural statement) and is not limited to the Penal Code: item 16 lists the Penal Code 1871 as a whole.
--
-- The Schedule as printed has 32 items; two carry a qualification (items 2A and 9) and one the Act's own qualifier (item 18).  The Minister
-- may amend the Schedule (s 427(1)); orders after 01 Oct 2026 are not applied.
--
-- Item 12 (Misuse of Drugs Act 1973) and item 16A (Prevention of Corruption Act 1960) are the two Acts encoded in their own subjects (sg/misuse-of-drugs-act-1973,
-- sg/prevention-of-corruption-act-1960).  Neither Act's offences are read here: cpc-other-laws.l4 reads the Act's statement about its own offences, and builds the
-- `Written Law Offence Facts` this module's rules take from it (`the written law offence facts for the Act's offence`).

§ `The Second Schedule`

-- item   Act (the short title)   Act as printed   qualification
@ref "Criminal Procedure Code 2010, Second Schedule, items 1 to 23"
`the Second Schedule` MEANS
    LIST
        (`Second Schedule Item` OF "1", "Arms and Explosives Act 1913", "Arms and Explosives Act 1913", "")
      , (`Second Schedule Item` OF "2", "Arms Offences Act 1973", "Arms Offences Act 1973", "")
      , (`Second Schedule Item` OF "2A", "Banishment Act 1959", "Banishment Act 1959 (as in force immediately before the date of commencement of section 61 of the Immigration (Amendment) Act 2023)", "as in force immediately before the date of commencement of section 61 of the Immigration (Amendment) Act 2023")
